WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:06.300
So we talked a couple of weeks ago about the
bad idea that is Michael Bloomberg running

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.300
for president.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:11.429
Michael Bloomberg is a billionaire, longtime
Republican turned Democrat.

00:00:11.429 --> 00:00:16.209
He owns the Bloomberg TV channel, the Bloomberg
news organization, and he is way, way richer

00:00:16.209 --> 00:00:17.820
than Trump.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:22.029
We don't know exactly how Trump, Richard is,
we, we assume he's exaggerating, but if Trump

00:00:22.029 --> 00:00:27.499
is a billionaire, Bloomberg is like a turbo
billionaire with a net worth reportedly of

00:00:27.499 --> 00:00:31.119
more than 54 billion us dollars.

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:34.470
We told you a couple of weeks ago, Bloomberg
was thinking about running for president.

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:37.800
He now is running for president as a Democrat
in the democratic primary.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.910
Now, according to the latest morning consult
poll, Bloomberg is already pulling 2% and

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:44.430
an average of recent polls.

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:50.400
Bloomberg is already pulling ahead of Tom
Stier, Amy Klobuchar, Cory Booker, who Leon

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:55.790
Castro and has tied Tulsi Gabard after just
a few days in the race.

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:58.670
That being said, Bloomberg obviously can't
win the primary.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:00:59.950
He's just, he's not going to win the primary.

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:00.950
There's no chance.

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:02.130
So what's going on here?

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:08.550
I believe that Michael Bloomberg is basically
trying to prevent Elizabeth Warren or Bernie

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:15.440
Sanders from becoming the democratic nominees
whose policies would directly affect Michael

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:18.600
Bloomberg potentially to the tune of billions
of dollars.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.030
I'll explain.

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:24.970
Bloomberg has said, defeating Donald Trump
is the most important thing, that that's the

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:25.970
priority.

00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:27.610
That's what made him consider running.

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:30.229
He believes Trump must be removed.

00:01:30.229 --> 00:01:35.180
And Tom Stire, another billionaire who's running
has said that exact same thing.

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:37.290
Now, Stier has a fraction of the money.

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:40.820
Bloomberg has styled reportedly worth around
a billion and a half.

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:45.170
Again, as I said before, Bloomberg worth about
$54 billion.

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:51.510
And I said about Tom Stiers, uh, candidacy
last week after the democratic debate.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:54.520
If you really want to defeat Trump, don't
run yourself.

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:55.520
You have no shot.

00:01:55.520 --> 00:02:01.260
Put the $50 million or however much Tom Stier
says he's willing to spend on his campaign,

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:07.990
put that money into defeating Trump by helping
somebody else put the money into voter registration

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:10.379
and into fighting voter suppression.

00:02:10.379 --> 00:02:16.769
Put it into a huge TV campaign to, um, uh,
antagonize Trump and support the eventual

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:18.269
democratic nominee.

00:02:18.269 --> 00:02:22.379
If Tom Stire is willing to spend 50 million
to defeat, Trump is the point.

00:02:22.379 --> 00:02:26.090
There are far better and more effective ways
to do it than by running himself.

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:27.150
Fine.

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:30.459
Bloomberg has nearly 50 times the money of
Tom Stier.

00:02:30.459 --> 00:02:37.349
If Bloomberg wants hurt Trump by Fox news
and stop the pro Trump propaganda, I've mentioned

00:02:37.349 --> 00:02:41.400
this before, I'm not literally saying buying
Fox news, I don't think it's for sale, but

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:46.800
the, the point is there are ways that Bloomberg
can take whatever amount of money he's willing

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.190
to spend on his campaign.

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:49.540
Maybe it's a billion of his own money.

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:51.319
Who knows?

00:02:51.319 --> 00:02:57.060
Spend it in other ways that will actually
help get rid of Donald Trump because Bloomberg's

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:58.700
not going to win.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:01.650
And that's where we get to the Bernie Warren
element of this.

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:07.080
If you go to Elizabeth Warren's wealth tax
calculator, and you put in Michael Bloomberg's

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:13.249
net worth, Michael Bloomberg would pay three
point $1 billion under Elizabeth Warren's

00:03:13.249 --> 00:03:14.249
wealth tax.

00:03:14.249 --> 00:03:18.249
So forget about the 50 million that Tom Stire
is spending.

00:03:18.249 --> 00:03:24.609
Even if Michael Bloomberg spent $1 billion,
it could prevent Warren from winning and save

00:03:24.609 --> 00:03:29.120
him an additional $2 billion in theory anyway.

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:30.739
Now of course let's be realistic.

00:03:30.739 --> 00:03:36.609
The wealth tax is not hugely likely to be
made law, even if Elizabeth Warren is president.

00:03:36.609 --> 00:03:43.230
I know that this is sort of taboo to talk
about on on some slices a amongst some circles

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:48.870
on the left, but a lot of the policies that
Bernie and Warren say they want will never

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:49.920
be made law.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:50.920
This is just a reality.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:52.389
This is the way that it works.

00:03:52.389 --> 00:03:55.919
You sort of say what it is, what it is that
you would like to do, and then you end up

00:03:55.919 --> 00:03:59.329
having to negotiate on almost all of those
issues merely to a fraction of that.

00:03:59.329 --> 00:04:03.769
So it's very likely that Warren's wealth tax
would not be made the law anyway, but there

00:04:03.769 --> 00:04:10.430
is no question that the policy ideas of Warren
and Bernie are a threat to Michael Bloomberg's

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:11.940
personal finances.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:19.060
And increasingly it seems that Bloomberg's
goal is run to prevent Warren or Bernie from

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:23.889
winning the primary and likely to keep Joe
Biden in the lead.

00:04:23.889 --> 00:04:26.900
Now this is logical behavior in a sense.

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:31.350
If you're Michael Bloomberg, from a personal
point of view, it does make sense.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:35.879
There's a practical reality though that I
think Bloomberg may be ignoring, which is

00:04:35.879 --> 00:04:42.620
any support Bloomberg can pull from the democratic
primary electorate is more likely to come

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:46.080
from Joe Biden and other centrist candidates.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:51.610
Then from Bernie, it's hard to imagine too
many Bernie voters saying, Oh, Michael Bloomberg's

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:54.340
running, I'm going to switch my vote from
Bernie to Bloomberg.

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:57.479
Similarly with Elizabeth Warren, it's hard
to imagine that.

00:04:57.479 --> 00:05:00.030
So I think it's a bad plan.

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:06.699
I don't think the numbers actually, uh, support
the idea that Bloomberg can prevent Bernie

00:05:06.699 --> 00:05:11.220
or Warren from taking the nomination unless
he's actually going to proactively go out

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:15.030
and spend money on smearing them, which we've
not seen yet, but maybe we'll start.

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:21.259
But I think it could just muddle things enough,
uh, that it still could prevent someone like

00:05:21.259 --> 00:05:26.740
Bernie Sanders or Warren from taking a solid
lead in the national democratic primary, which

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:31.180
so far with the exception of Elizabeth Warren
for a few days a month ago, uh, they have

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:32.310
been unable to do.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:34.620
It's a calculation that Michael Bloomberg
is doing.

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:36.150
I think it's a wrong calculation.

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:39.690
I think it's a calculation that's bad for
the country, but this is what I believe is

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:40.889
going on.

00:05:40.889 --> 00:05:41.889
Let me know what you think.

00:05:41.889 --> 00:05:43.159
I want to hear from you.

00:05:43.159 --> 00:05:49.189
What do you believe underlies this Bloomberg
candidacy because he's not going to win.

00:05:49.189 --> 00:05:53.050
Is it trying to keep Warren or Bernie from
being the nominee?

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:59.259
Is it as some people have emailed me merely
a nearly 80 year old Bloomberg who sees this

00:05:59.259 --> 00:06:04.210
as the best opportunity to make a bigger name
for himself.

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:09.830
He has a lot of money, but maybe not as well
known of a celebrity rich dude as he would

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:10.830
like to be.

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:11.830
Is it merely that?

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:13.780
Is it something else I want to hear from you?

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:16.280
Let me know either by leaving a comment on
this

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:17.520
YouTube channel video.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:21.990
If you're watching on the YouTube channel
or by sending me a tweet at the Pacman.

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:22.990
What is Michael Bloomberg?

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:22.996
Really up to deep down here,

